Have you checked the debugging guide <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/user%3Ermr%3EDebugging-rmr-programs>? I always start developing on the local backend, with local input files. Then you could call debug(tfM.map), rerun your program and see what happens line by line. If i understand right, the paste is the only difference between working program and failing program. So it must be recycling happening there, then interacting with recycling in the keyval function. What else could it be? Finally, there is nothing like allowing me to run this program by myself. I have the relevant functions. I need the output of

dump(wm, stdout())
dump(tfM.map_out, stdout())

That way I should be able to run the reduce phase. Thanks

Antonio

